---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE OF THE ABOVE

The notice above covers the work done here: the migration to Animal Apparel:
Framework, the AnimalNeck body part group and its body patch, the rewritten
horse gear defs, and the French translation.

It does NOT relicense the content that came from other people's mods. Their
status is set out one by one in ATTRIBUTION.md. In short:

  - Animal Equipment, by Owlchemist, is MIT, and its notice is reproduced
    below because the MIT licence requires it to travel with the work.
  - No licence has been identified for the other six source mods in the
    installed Workshop files and accessible public descriptions checked on
    2026-09-12. Some public pages could not be reverified. No permission for
    their reuse in this project has been established, and their abandonment
    has not been established in every case.
    Credit and removal on request are project commitments, not licence grants
    from those authors. Nothing here relicenses their contributions or claims
    ownership of their art or designs.


---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ANIMAL EQUIPMENT — the original authors' notice

Reproduced verbatim from github.com/Owlchemist/animal-equipment, which is the
source of the animal clothing, headwear, riding gear and power armour, of the
research chain they hang off, and of the universal "placeholder" pieces. The
copyright line is jptrrs's: Animal Equipment is Owlchemist's continuation of
jptrrs's Animal Armor: Vanilla, and the file was carried forward unchanged.

